flowchart TD
    REVIEW["Required human/governance approvals<br/>before authoritative publication"]
    REVIEW --> PUB["Publish approved Fabric SQL configuration<br/>Complete immutable snapshot; candidate semver before CI"]
    PUB --> QUEUE["Automatically enqueue corresponding DAG release<br/>No second manual release approval"]
    QUEUE --> NEXT["Sequential worker selects next approved release<br/>Queue/claim schema and trigger mechanism pending"]
    NEXT --> GEN["Generate from this release's full snapshot and code revision<br/>Framework and DAG artifact share semantic version"]
    GEN --> CHECK["Required CI and technical validation<br/>Graph, functions, tasks, datasets, resource maps and artifacts"]
    CHECK --> DEPLOY["Deploy candidate DAG artifact<br/>Artifact/pinning/activation mechanisms pending"]
    DEPLOY --> RECOGNIZE["Verify Airflow recognition and required deployment health<br/>Recognition failure is not activation"]
    RECOGNIZE --> ACTIVE["Activate successful immutable release<br/>New runs bind latest active; published does not mean active"]
    ACTIVE --> SUCCESS["Record active version and evidence<br/>In-flight runs retain original version/configuration"]
    GEN -- Failure --> FAIL["Record failed release and diagnostics; alert<br/>Do not label it successfully deployed"]
    CHECK -- Failure --> FAIL
    DEPLOY -- Failure --> FAIL
    RECOGNIZE -- Failure --> FAIL
    FAIL --> KEEP["Failed candidate keeps last-good active deployment<br/>Do not deploy repaired obsolete versions over newer active ones"]
    KEEP --> NEXT
    SUCCESS --> NEXT
    EXAMPLE["Example only: active 1.1.0; failed 1.1.1; active 1.2.0<br/>Normally fix on latest as 1.2.1, not repaired older 1.1.1"]
    KEEP -. Later queued release may proceed .-> EXAMPLE
    ACTIVE --> HEALTH{"Post-activation incident class?"}
    HEALTH -- Defined technical health failure --> AUTO["Automatic rollback under approved health rules"]
    HEALTH -- Suspected data-quality or clinical issue --> OPERATOR["Operator review and approval required"]
    AUTO --> ROLLBACK["Reactivate immutable last-known-good for NEW runs<br/>Audit transition; no Delta undo or silent in-flight cancellation"]
    OPERATOR -- Authorized --> ROLLBACK
    ROLLBACK --> PATCH["Fix forward in a new patch; review and validate normally<br/>Example only: 1.3.0 to known-good 1.2.3, then tested 1.3.1"]
    PATCH --> REVIEW
    NOTE["Conceptual lifecycle; exact activation/pinning/rollback mechanisms pending<br/>Initial design/environment/infrastructure approvals still apply"]
    NOTE -. Boundary .-> PUB
